#===----------------------------------------------------------------------===#
#
# The ruleset the C++ style judge holds generated C++ to.
#
# Read by tools/judge_generated_code.py, which passes it with --config-file.
# It is the project's own .clang-tidy applied to what dsdlc writes: whole
# families are enabled, and a check is subtracted only for a reason that holds
# for generated code. Where the project's reason does not carry over, the check
# stays on.
#
# Subtractions
# ------------
#
# bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#     Fires on the plan's helpers, whose operands are `std::uint64_t` in the
#     order the IR gives them, and on the runtime's accessors, which take a
#     buffer's size beside a bit offset.
#
# cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers, readability-magic-numbers
#     Bit widths, field offsets, and wire-format constants are the subject
#     matter.
#
# cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
# misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes
#     A generated type is data, and its public members are the DSDL fields.
#
# cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
# cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index,
# cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic
#     Serialisation walks buffers by pointer and indexes them unchecked. The
#     bounds come from the BitLengthSet algebra.
#
# modernize-use-trailing-return-type
#     The generated C++ writes leading return types, as the project's own does.
#
# readability-function-cognitive-complexity
#     A body branches where its plan does, and the plan is held by the
#     round-trip, parity, and equivalence lanes.
#
# readability-identifier-length
#     A length floor is a convention of neither C nor C++, and no other
#     language's judge holds its output to one.
#
# cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast stays on although the project
# subtracts it for type punning. The generated C++ puns nothing: its one
# reinterpret_cast turns a string literal into a byte pointer to stand in for a
# null buffer.
#
# Naming
# ------
#
# readability-identifier-naming states the design in CLEAN_CODE.md: namespaces
# in lower_case, types in CamelCase, functions, fields, parameters, and locals
# in lower_case, and a type's facts and constants in UPPER_CASE. No option
# excepts the way the output composes names today, so `List_Request` and
# `List_Request_serialize_` are findings until the C++ phase nests them.
#
# A namespace or member ending in `_` is a DSDL name as its author spelt it or
# as the generator strops a keyword, or a member the generator adds beside the
# fields. An added member takes the form DSDL reserves, starting and ending
# with an underscore, so no field can take its name: `_tag_`.
#
# Editing
# -------
#
# Keep `#` out of the `Checks:` scalar; .clang-tidy says why.
# tools/check_clang_tidy_config.py runs over this file in the Lint job.
#
#===----------------------------------------------------------------------===#
---
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  concurrency-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  misc-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-magic-numbers

CheckOptions:
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassConstantCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstexprVariableCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.EnumCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.EnumConstantCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.FunctionCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.MacroDefinitionCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.MemberCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.MemberIgnoredRegexp: '^_?[a-z][a-z0-9_]*_$'
  readability-identifier-naming.MethodCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceIgnoredRegexp: '^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*_$'
  readability-identifier-naming.ParameterCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.StructCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TemplateParameterCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TypeAliasCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TypedefCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.UnionCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.VariableCase: lower_case
